{pad:ignore}
<p><code>{pad:oauth 'github'/}</code> is the link that starts a login at GitHub, styled as a button with
the provider's name - and its icon, when the icon set has one of its name. It goes to the page
<code>oauth/github</code> of the application unless <code>href=</code> names another: one page,
<code>oauth/[provider].php</code>, serves every provider - <code>padOAuthStart ( $provider )</code>
sends the visitor off with a state, a PKCE challenge and (OpenID Connect) a nonce kept in the
session, and on the way back <code>padOAuthUser ( $provider )</code> checks the state, exchanges the
code, checks the id_token and answers the user for <code>padLogin</code>.</p>

<p>The button reads no setting and makes no request; the page it links to needs the client id and
secret - <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET</code> in <code>.env</code>. An
unknown provider is an error under the strict check.</p>
{/pad:ignore}

<h3>OAuth providers</h3>
